th} :answer/value "x+3y-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423953} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5c8545-4573-5ed8-bdbb-b47cb8a05b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+3y-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423954} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e87eac-968b-5331-95b6-4aa94e8c328b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y+z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423956} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y-5z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423958} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc839475-9e1b-518e-9233-6715536351ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3a2e450-d136-5240-a920-568065ef68bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-33146" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(0,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-3}{1}=\\frac{z}{5}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,2,1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,1,5⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =⟨0,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z-7 & =0 \\\\ 2x-y-5z+7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ed62a8-9b3b-51e5-ac43-d4da0a1c1543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s⟨1,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,-0.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410862} {:answer/id #uuid "18ac7d09-6c6c-56d5-bca5-deff31cfa6a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,3,0⟩+s⟨1,-1,3⟩+t⟨0,2,-0.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410863} {:answer/id #uuid "2460749d-a40c-5994-b70c-3b47f527aae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,2,-0.5⟩+s⟨1,3,0⟩+t⟨1,-1,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410866} {:answer/id #uuid "81225de3-3d45-5766-b3a3-0475567dc5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410880} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d064a4-78fb-5cc5-a4e6-a121e1f4b2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,-1,3⟩+s⟨1,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,-0.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410884}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410884} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4562dcb-eeb1-5126-82bd-cc20dbf44d99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "001b7edd-c428-5436-8d89-3502541770a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-33154" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-1,3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨1,3,0⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,-0.5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $p=⟨1,-1,3⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨1,3,0⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,-0.5⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,-1,3⟩+s⟨1,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,-0.5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f8ebc88-3678-5a9c-9729-113000b44300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} + s\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117570} {:answer/id #uuid "b6986c57-94d2-5de3-93dc-8588be5327de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117571} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a6a636-e02f-509b-83dc-1a48ced9af10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix} + s\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117572} {:answer/id #uuid "06fb47f5-1cbb-58b0-a446-8575654b932b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117573} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc004d4-89df-58b7-bcb8-f4d711d8ba92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = s\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117574}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e9aa72b3-fddd-5fbc-99d8-05282ddde5ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117569}] :question/id #uuid "142b5f50-b3b0-5007-a86c-38ef279cec00" :question/math-academy-id "q-33155" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(4,-3, \\sqrt{2})$ and is parallel to the vectors $v_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2646d87e-2e74-5757-bc34-02f20d6114fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302705} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff6b838-1af4-5c00-868a-734468c82814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨-30,55,25⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303040} {:answer/id #uuid "68558628-ae8a-519a-9cf8-9a1b1e7f6286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303091} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a9c33e-fe94-5b43-8ee0-a43a2a47c5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303676} {:answer/id #uuid "e74734b6-d893-59de-a060-0512213f4bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,5,4⟩+s⟨-2,23,14⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303894}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302705} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f249d4-cd35-55dd-9318-5acc4887eb5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88872368-686b-5e7f-9016-e33ff5ee0ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33158" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-2,23,14)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-3,5,1⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $r=⟨-30,55,25⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨4,7,-1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-2,23,14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-2,23,14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a569713-1980-5360-a5a7-e64596f5fef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+3y-z-42=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303007} {:answer/id #uuid "9793b331-23e7-53ab-a79a-90019f4af6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+y+2z-42=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303398} {:answer/id #uuid "dd7b10d6-e284-5047-ac5a-3540420c0f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+3y-z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303842} {:answer/id #uuid "f605912d-f296-5e78-b0e3-1cfdef5c5a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x+y+2z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304003} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb41d38-6777-5b29-9db2-82a1b459da22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+3y-z-42=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304036}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304036} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e617e69-db16-53f5-ac12-a24c8d9c3852" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0dec6df-1301-5550-8bf9-7363cae85702" :question/math-academy-id "q-33165" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(8,3,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{x+2}{4}=\\frac{y-1}{3}=\\frac{z-2}{-1}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨8,3,-1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,3,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨4,3,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =⟨8,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,-1⟩ & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z & =42 \\\\ 4x+3y-z-42 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c2e5ca-f263-54ef-924a-e167ca91f89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,0⟩=⟨-4,6,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363753} {:answer/id #uuid "32d8e4c3-ddfe-54ee-ae03-e8de00c5efb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,0⟩=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363754} {:answer/id #uuid "730f759e-812a-532c-8ba9-65f2916ee485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363755} {:answer/id #uuid "9471d411-f775-5f03-a79f-1eb639079ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363756} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6058f7-7b71-5d3e-a88e-644aa57521b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=⟨-2,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363755} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ab60fb-0ccd-54c4-b8b9-1cf65f373926" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a0ae68a-8650-5549-af6c-052d2786d395" :question/math-academy-id "q-33316" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-2,2,0)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-4t \\\\ y &=1+6t \\\\ z &=-1+2t.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-2,2,0⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-4t \\\\ y &=1+6t \\\\ z &=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨3,1,-1⟩+t\\text{ }\\underbrace{⟨-4,6,2⟩}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-4,6,2⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-4,6,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ & =⟨-2,2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4846e6-07fa-5199-92fa-c23138fb6c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305727} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1bb14c-5955-581a-b7ba-96cdefb1c303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306012} {:answer/id #uuid "74c26a6c-96c5-502a-b012-f87b7a57e25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306261} {:answer/id #uuid "7914febd-cdaa-5378-9536-eea1bae6ff8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306305} {:answer/id #uuid "8c64b39c-1d55-5de4-bd2e-bb1289db7f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306485}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306261} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1987b64-0643-52df-ab2f-a1e652a8c54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d32af589-36a2-5da2-a4fd-d2edd8386949" :question/math-academy-id "q-33319" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc5a327-948f-52bc-9425-a1da5c008b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3, \\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117802} {:answer/id #uuid "1ad1ef08-8e25-56d5-81a4-d8415b600831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-20,-21⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117803} {:answer/id #uuid "466567c6-7d78-5c8f-bcbc-e93fb9a1922a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 34,-14, 11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117804} {:answer/id #uuid "520486a4-098a-554d-aaba-77c2dbbe8a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-4, 3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117805} {:answer/id #uuid "768cf5fc-fd19-53e6-9c22-78654b2744df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 43,-11, 14⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117806}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5be3308d-6e28-5a8a-ae4d-0380fed569a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a44a633c-f708-59a5-ba3d-1849b40eba40" :question/math-academy-id "q-33816" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n$$\n\\displaystyle r = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}, t, s ∈ (- ∞, ∞).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b5e92d-6224-56f5-944e-a8b83ad251a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-59,10,-20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308877} {:answer/id #uuid "719fd09d-d078-59ed-81b8-c5e456b9a391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-95,20,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309632} {:answer/id #uuid "740f86a3-b4cf-5219-84a0-d82570a20efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309648} {:answer/id #uuid "90ffb081-cc79-57a0-a759-a970dcf68248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-84,25⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309908} {:answer/id #uuid "b018f396-0291-53b4-b697-3ecdf0cb89a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-7,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309632} :answer-field/id #uuid "121b2d9e-6258-5ba0-b2c8-a9ee055f9a6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "183d75ab-bc55-5284-9356-4879f8cd6310" :question/math-academy-id "q-33818" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,0,-1⟩+t⟨-2,-7,5⟩+s⟨2,12,5⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,-7,5⟩$ and $w=⟨2,12,5⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-95i+20j-10k \\\\  & =⟨-95,20,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-95,20,-10⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c147174b-1e66-5bb1-8e90-13814203679e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r - ⟨0, 0,-11⟩) \\cdot ⟨1, 3, 1⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117832} {:answer/id #uuid "d67d2b5f-fede-5695-9b57-a3bf50396308" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r - ⟨0, 0, 11⟩) \\cdot ⟨ - 3, 1, 1⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117833} {:answer/id #uuid "efb55b6a-d8c7-500a-b6f7-0d6c187cceb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r - ⟨0, 0,-11⟩) \\cdot ⟨1,-3, 1⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117834} {:answer/id #uuid "6665d96e-fec2-578e-a9c9-f2cbc92cbb45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r - ⟨0, 0,-11⟩) \\cdot ⟨0,-3, 0⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117835} {:answer/id #uuid "69727246-18cc-5acd-9b31-f362752065f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r - ⟨0, 0, 11⟩) \\cdot ⟨1,-3, 1⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117836}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5e55607d-6cce-5bdc-89f8-814be1f46e74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117831}] :question/id #uuid "2f27f995-465d-53e3-bd9f-87302aae4193" :question/math-academy-id "q-33911" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $x - 3y + z + 11 = 0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r - p) \\cdot n = 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bf34d07-cd99-5983-8a1b-cb31892f721e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-2y+z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312064} {:answer/id #uuid "543cf762-98f0-583c-b80f-a17527258a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-5y+5z-16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312656} {:answer/id #uuid "81d82da8-094c-5d53-92cb-5fda4924d683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-5y+5z=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313021} {:answer/id #uuid "869b5aba-db3e-5905-b9d5-c7f7146ea7fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-2y+z+16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313053} {:answer/id #uuid "d14dfaa9-4c8e-55a3-b867-d30669e90de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+5y+5z+16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313609}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312656} :answer-field/id #uuid "9200a78c-c2dd-5fc5-8cd7-e5930b0a22e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93f0f0ea-5609-5473-8b26-f85225442381" :question/math-academy-id "q-33912" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,0,3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨5,2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,3,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨1,0,3⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3i-15j+15k \\\\  & =⟨3,-15,15⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-15,15⟩ & =⟨1,0,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-15,15⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-15,15⟩ & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-15,15⟩ & =48 \\\\ 3x-15y+15z & =48 \\\\ 3x-15y+15z-48 & =0 \\\\ x-5y+5z-16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7132a908-b9cb-56e3-80b1-38fb5d14b3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,-1,16⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391743} {:answer/id #uuid "02494726-37b0-5e7b-ad3c-0180bececdfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391744} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ff3e24-bbb2-547d-9f0d-bbf347c313df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391745} {:answer/id #uuid "ef59ef21-d4e1-5b2a-82ab-a424aa93aa72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391746} {:answer/id #uuid "875a9589-3b53-5b62-afd7-0ad0dc57bbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391744} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0ed6f5-6be8-59e5-9f66-3f6c05ef700b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d949e3c-e35b-5754-bfa5-04230aa782a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33923" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $x-y+4z+16=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-1,4⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+4z+16 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}y-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-4.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-4)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-4⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-1,4⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe2d5e-1c5c-577a-a451-998f8106110f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 6z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117850} {:answer/id #uuid "dc762087-1251-5369-a326-070c955ec5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + y - z + 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117851} {:answer/id #uuid "2becb369-29f3-530a-a830-67072d6603d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + y - z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117852} {:answer/id #uuid "5278345a-02bb-5d0d-aef9-f66af8da55f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 6z + 5 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117853} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3c126e-d453-502b-9381-9c539972498d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + y - z = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117854}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0fbde03e-a986-5a0b-8d66-d9a9c8968c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117849}] :question/id #uuid "1b440376-e325-5242-bbb9-dcbb8b153081" :question/math-academy-id "q-33931" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1, 0, 6)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n = ⟨1, 1,-1⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30f92df8-451b-5c89-afe4-2baa87ea99f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336501} {:answer/id #uuid "6e834384-8f29-5ff4-9222-0f7a9f6994fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337012} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1f431b-0e82-51f2-ba39-70abbb308701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337291} {:answer/id #uuid "dd802b6b-b301-5612-8ca6-ffbbd614fa35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337959} {:answer/id #uuid "f8454c79-6668-58ba-8cdc-97692e6243bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338208}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337012} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d6e4be-5b5b-5868-8505-0ae308184b08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1725487-2c6d-5d22-95bb-183dbe4038eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-70821" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩=-12.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation of the plane, $r\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩=-12,$  we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,-3,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}-3{t}_{2}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{2}-3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},3{t}_{2}-3{t}_{1}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{1}{-3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192504 :question/id #uuid "32f7b0e6-5a68-52ab-9d86-ea71387cfb77" :question/math-academy-id "e-10975" :question/problem "![](images/72/72329ee334988361174013e7df57452851cd826acf2ffc8b4cead6d750683e73.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of $\\mathbb{R}^2?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I represents the whole plane $\\mathbb{R}^2$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin. Therefore, it is *not* a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^2.$\n\n- Diagram II is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^2.$\n\n- Diagram III is a parabola that does not pass through the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin. Therefore, it is *not* a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^2.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192505 :question/id #uuid "554fc7b1-62ca-5189-bda1-712f518ad617" :question/math-academy-id "e-10976" :question/problem "Consider the subsets $\\; A=\\{ \\langle x, y, z \\rangle \\in \\mathbb{R}^3 : x^2=y \\}\\;$ and $\\; B= \\{ \\langle 3-t, -3+t, -6+2t \\rangle : t \\in \\mathbb{R} \\}.\\;$ Which of them is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it is not closed under scalar multiplication. For example, the vector $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}$ belongs to $A,$ but the vector $2\\cdot \\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}$ does not lie in $A$ (because it does not satisfy $x^2=y$).\n\n- The set $B$ represents a line, and a line is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. If the origin belongs to this subset, we would have\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}3 - t \\\\ - 3 + t \\\\ - 6 + 2 t\\end{array} \\right]}=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]},\n$$\nwhich gives us\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3-t &=0 \\\\ -3+t &=0 \\\\ -6+2t &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe see that $t=3$ is the solution to the three equations. So, if we choose $t=3,$ then we find that $\\mathbf{0} \\in B.$ Therefore, $B$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192506 :question/id #uuid "6e80df98-c67c-5f27-a44b-d0bc8f681ac6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10979" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c66cdc8bbddfb00ce69f843b1ce1d12116b2dd82312a34abafa0fb13907110cf.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of $\\mathbb{R}^3?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I  represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram II  represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is also a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $\\mathbf{0}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{array} \\right]}$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e86471bd-e6c5-5896-af8e-c48e8e06dc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459811} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae10483-1250-5ee8-a5b7-56019635b6ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459812}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459811} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3e684d-5745-5881-b7a9-0cb4fc6b3e66" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/e7/e79e96039bc2ebbe1787345b90a84e42e7410c0ef500dfac37844bdc1a10e756.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ae8346-7f12-51b2-8e39-86863fc03e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459813} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7012c9-36fc-589a-9d2d-cf11e2f8491f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459813} :answer-field/id #uuid "d610899c-18de-528a-ad41-0903543b7fb2" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/76/7655da5d10b7ace907bd613342d576a691451532aaa7564a9e17c1b41a66097b.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b69ec572-d020-59f8-83a0-b46528d98a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459815} {:answer/id #uuid "54b24640-ac48-5b77-ab4e-3e63e4bf019d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459815} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a6b85af-a931-557d-a8f0-f8d4434ad92c" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/f0/f04fb553eed6853549b0aa6c0f03b05e7f69931d8ba1cfaf0cef2486c82820d7.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef4f5c5f-3398-5540-9361-58d558e57438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668028} {:answer/id #uuid "184312d5-c485-5c3b-9c21-9aefbffac05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668029}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186668029} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4c7d69-bad2-55ff-b22f-784b6f1a7741" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "028630ef-e1bc-5d42-ac61-af7d94939f1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-34318" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside given subset. But\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace since in does not contain the zero-vector.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a555ac6b-b16f-53ec-865a-a31c99ba4